  Title: Late bedtimes are linked to higher heart disease risk
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260130041101.htm
  Category: research
  importance: 80
  ai_summary: "A large study reveals that individuals who consistently stay up late have a higher risk of heart disease, particularly in middle-aged and older adults, with a notable impact on women."
  
  Title: New scan spots heart disease years before symptoms
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260129080954.htm
  Category: research
  importance: 75
  ai_summary: "A novel imaging technique called fast-RSOM can detect early signs of heart disease by visualizing small blood vessels, potentially years before symptoms manifest."
  
  Title: The early turning point when men’s heart risk accelerates
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260130041056.htm
  Category: research
  importance: 70
  ai_summary: "Research indicates that men's risk of heart disease begins to accelerate around age 35, driven primarily by coronary heart disease, suggesting the need for earlier screening."
  
  Title: A quiet change in everyday foods could save thousands of lives
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260131082433.htm
  Category: research
  importance: 65
  ai_summary: "Modestly reducing sodium in common foods like bread and packaged meals could significantly lower heart disease and stroke rates without requiring changes to eating habits."


